{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/8BD721F397/": {
      "title": "Nursing Student Support Specialist, Part-Time",
      "description": "Nursing Student Support Specialist, Part-Time. Academic Affairs / School of Health Sciences / Nursing and Public Health The Nursing Student Support Specialist is a part-time position responsible for leading academic support and student success initiatives for nursing students, with a focus on academic progression, retention, individualized student support, and NCLEX readiness. This position collaborates with students, faculty, and campus partners to identify needs, provide student resources and intervention, and support student success throughout the nursing program. POSITION STATUS: This is a non-exempt, half-time position requiring in-person work for approximately 20 hours per week (Monday-Friday) from August through May. Hours are limited in June and July, with a minimum commitment of 5-10 hours of work per week and 1,040 hours per year. This position is not eligible for remote work. Salary Range: $27.50 - $30.00. This is the expected hourly range for this position. The hourly range offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Responsibilities Manages academic support programming and student success initiatives for undergraduate nursing students across all years of the program, providing proactive outreach to students identified at risk. Analyzes academic performance and progression data to identify students in need of early intervention and develop strategies to improve student outcomes and retention. Provides individualized academic support and coaching to students experiencing academic challenges, including development of academic success plans and referrals to appropriate campus resources in collaboration with students’ faculty advisors, program leadership, academic advising, student accessibility services, and other campus partners. Maintains a systematic student-success caseload, documenting interventions, monitoring outcomes, and closing the loop on referrals. Manages the NCLEX eligibility and application process, ensuring required paperwork and documentation are completed and submitted accurately and on time so students are approved to sit for the licensure examination. Monitors and maintains clinical feedback forms and Student Individualized Education Plans (SIEPs), tracking student progress and ensuring timely follow-up, documentation, and communication with faculty and students. Develops and delivers small- and large-group student workshops on topics including study strategies, time management, test-taking, clinical preparation, learning science, stress management, and preparation for nursing licensure examinations. Schedules and deploys course evaluations, compiles student feedback on courses and clinicals, and distributes evaluative data to course faculty. Evaluates the effectiveness of student-success initiatives using student performance, progression, retention, and graduation data, and prepares reports and makes recommendations for improvement. Other Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Supports the mission, vision, and values of Elmhurst University. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications BSN graduate holding current Illinois RN licensure. 3+ years of experience working with undergraduate nursing students or in academic/student support within a higher education or healthcare setting. Demonstrated experience providing academic advising, coaching, student support, or early intervention to undergraduate students. Experience interpreting academic data and using it to identify students who may be at risk academically or of delayed progression. Experience developing and facilitating individual and group academic support programs. Strong organizational skills and experience managing confidential student records and documentation. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Proficiency with student information systems, Microsoft Office, and data tracking/reporting tools. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with NCLEX preparation, NCLEX eligibility/application processes, or nursing licensure requirements. Experience working with clinical education, including reviewing clinical evaluations/feedback and monitoring student progression. Knowledge of nursing curricula, clinical education, accreditation requirements, and student progression policies. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here ."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/0470DD89C5/": {
      "title": "Building Access Technician",
      "description": "Building Access Technician. Facilities Management As a member of the Building Maintenance team, the Building Access Technician is responsible for the installation, maintenance, repair, troubleshooting, and documentation of physical access infrastructure. This position performs skilled carpentry work involving door installation and repair as well as locksmith work involving mechanical and electronic locking systems, key and credential management, access control systems, alarms, security cameras, and related door hardware. The Building Access Technician supports a safe and secure campus environment through preventative maintenance, emergency response, system administration, and collaboration with Facilities Management colleagues and the Public Safety team. Position Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $26.50 - $28.50. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. The actual salary offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. REPORTING AND SUPERVISORY RELATIONSHIP(S): Direct reporting relationship to: Building Maintenance Supervisor Responsibilities Installs doors and frames, shortens steel and wooden doors, and resets or repairs thresholds using expansion anchors and cement drills. Performs carpentry work in the alteration, repair, remodeling, and maintenance of new and existing structures and areas, indoors and outdoors. Patches and paints of all types of building surfaces, interior and exterior. Performs preventive maintenance of locks, locking systems, door hardware, access control devices, alarms, and related equipment and reports all needed repairs in a timely fashion. Performs locksmith duties including the installation, maintenance, repair, replacement, and rekeying of mechanical and electronic locks, cylinders, keys, and door and cabinet hardware. Maintains key control records, access control databases, system documentation, and related security records. Collaborates with Public Safety, Facilities Management, Information Services, contractors, and other campus stakeholders to ensure the integrity and effectiveness of security systems. Assists with estimates of time and materials for all jobs. Supervises student employees and outside tradesmen occasionally, when required. Ensures all work is performed in accordance with applicable safety standards, building codes, manufacturer specifications, and University policies. Other Duties and Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Supports the University’s mission, vision and values. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications 2 to 3 years of experience in carpentry, locksmithing, electronic security systems, or a related field. Working knowledge of mechanical and electronic locks, key systems, door hardware, and security systems. Ability to handle and manipulate heavy and sometimes awkward materials, such as hanging of drywall and doors and installation of shelving units. Ability to work independently, prioritize assignments, and manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Strong interpersonal, customer service, and communication skills. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications Completion of a locksmith apprenticeship, locksmith certification program, electronics trade school, or equivalent technical training. Associate degree in Electronics, Electrical Technology, Security Systems Technology, or a related field. Certified Locksmith designation through a recognized professional organization. Experience in higher education, healthcare, government, or large institutional facilities. Work Hours 7:00 am – 3:30 pm, Monday through Friday, with possibility of emergency call in and weekend duties for special events, e.g., move-in weekend. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position require regular movement between indoor and outdoor campus locations, with exposure to varying weather conditions, including extreme heat and cold. Work is often physically demanding in nature and may require walking, navigating uneven or slippery surfaces, climbing stairs and ladders, bending, kneeling, and standing for extended periods. Required abilities include frequent use of fine motor skills to push, pull, or maneuver a range of equipment. Work requires regular lifting of objects up to 50 pounds, and occasional lifting of up to 100 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Instructions to Applicants This position is designated by Elmhurst University as being safety sensitive. Per University policy, candidates for employment in safety-sensitive positions must comply with pre-employment drug testing, and employment in these positions is contingent upon completion of a drug test with satisfactory results. With consideration for the working conditions and physical requirements for this position, as described in the section above, a physical examination is required as well. Both the drug testing and physical examination are conducted at the University’s expense in an approved facility within one week of acceptance of a written offer of employment. Candidates may communicate with the testing facility and with Human Resources to explain any positive test results. For additional information regarding this policy, candidates may email Human Resources at hr@elmhurst.edu for assistance"
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/8B5287A0F0/": {
      "title": "Philanthropy Officer/Senior Philanthropy Officer (2 openings)",
      "description": "Philanthropy Officer/Senior Philanthropy Officer (2 openings). Institutional Advancement POSITION TITLE(S): Philanthropy Officer/Senior Philanthropy Officer (2 openings) Title commensurate with experience and demonstrated fundraising success. Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Philanthropy Officer/Senior Philanthropy Officer is a direct fundraiser responsible for advancing meaningful relationships with donors, developing tailored engagement and solicitation strategies, and securing philanthropic commitments for scholarships, academic programs, capital projects, and other University priorities. The position manages a portfolio of donors and prospects capable of making major gifts of $10,000 or more and develops individualized strategies to identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward philanthropic support. The position collaborates with advancement colleagues, University leadership, and campus partners to strengthen the donor pipeline and advance the University’s mission. The Senior Philanthropy Officer is distinguished by demonstrated success managing a major or planned gift portfolio and greater independence in developing and executing complex donor strategies. Position Status: Exempt Reporting Relationship(s): Vice President for Institutional Advancement Salary Range: Philanthropy Officer: $75,000-$80,000. Senior Philanthropy Officer: $85,000-$90,000. These are the expected salary ranges for these positions. Appointment level and actual salary offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Responsibilities Manages a portfolio of major gift donors and prospects with the capacity to make gifts of $10,000 or more, ensuring consistent cultivation, solicitation, stewardship, and pipeline development activities. Conducts in-person visits, virtual meetings, phone calls, and written communications to build and sustain meaningful relationships with alumni, donors, parents, and friends of the University. Builds and maintains a robust major gift pipeline through prospect identification, qualification, referrals, data-informed prospecting, and engagement activities. Advances prospects through the fundraising cycle and achieves annual fundraising, donor contact, and portfolio activity goals established by the Vice President for Institutional Advancement. Prepares donor briefings, gift proposals, solicitation strategies, meeting materials, and other communications that support cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship efforts in collaboration with advancement leadership and campus partners. Collaborates with colleagues across the Office of Institutional Advancement and key University leaders, faculty, athletics, and student affairs to coordinate prospect strategies, fundraising initiatives, and donor engagement opportunities. Maintains consistent and proactive communication with donors and prospects, including timely follow-up on inquiries, meetings, gift acknowledgments, and stewardship activities. Maintains accurate, timely, and comprehensive documentation of prospect activity, strategies, and outcomes in the University's CRM system, Raiser’s Edge NXT. Initiates and facilitates conversations regarding planned giving opportunities with portfolio and non-portfolio donors, as appropriate. Participates in advancement events, donor engagement activities, and University programs, including evenings and weekends as needed. Supports campaign initiatives and other strategic fundraising priorities as assigned. Represents Elmhurst University professionally with alumni, donors, community partners, and other external stakeholders and maintains current knowledge of institutional priorities, goals, and initiatives. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Supports mission, vision and values of Elmhurst University. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Performs other duties and completes special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Philanthropy Officer Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 2 years of progressively responsible fundraising or related experience, with demonstrated experience building donor relationships. Major gift fundraising experience preferred. Ability to manage a portfolio of relationships, move donors or prospects toward increased engagement and philanthropic support, and consistently execute follow up and next steps. Senior Philanthropy Officer Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 5 years of proven major gift fundraising experience, preferably in higher education. Demonstrated success in cultivating, soliciting, and closing major or planned gifts. Demonstrated ability to independently manage a major gift portfolio and develop sophisticated donor strategies. Experience working effectively with senior leaders and other partners in donor cultivation and solicitation. Both Levels Strong interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills, with the ability to engage diverse donor constituencies. Knowledge of donor stewardship strategies and moves management systems. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, fundraising CRMs (such as Raiser’s Edge NXT), and prospect management tools. Excellent organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team-oriented environment. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Willingness to travel and engage in evening and weekend donor activities as needed. Preferred Qualifications Belief in and the ability to represent the Elmhurst University mission and core values. Experience in higher education or large nonprofit fundraising or comprehensive campaign environments. Experience collaborating with academic leaders, volunteers, and institutional leadership in fundraising efforts. Understanding of donor pipeline development strategies. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Please submit cover letter, resume, and three references with contact information with online application. The references should include name, phone number and email."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/E0FAD8511C/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychology (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Psychology (Tenure Track). Academic Affairs / School of Science, Technology and Mathematics / Psychology The Department of Psychology at Elmhurst University invites applications for a tenure-track, assistant professor position with an emphasis in Cognitive Neuroscience, broadly defined, beginning August 2027. The successful candidate will have demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring, and outstanding potential as a professor in a comprehensive liberal arts setting. The candidate will need to teach upper-level courses related to their area of expertise (including Cognitive Neuroscience), as well as lower-level methodology courses (such as Research Methods in Psychology), and other courses depending on candidate ability and department need as part of a 3/3 load. Preference will be given to candidates who can adapt their research program to a small, liberal arts environment and involve undergraduate students in their research. In addition, faculty are expected to contribute to the Department and University through service activities and advising. The Department of Psychology serves hundreds of majors and minors, participates in the university’s core curriculum, and supports other programs of study including the nursing program and the new neuroscience major. Candidate materials should demonstrate their commitment to creating an inclusive learning environment for a diverse student body. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in psychology (or a related field, e.g., neuroscience); however, ABD with significant progress towards the degree and a completion date prior to August 2027 will also be considered. ABD candidates should address this concern in their materials. Interested candidates must apply online by clicking the \"Apply for this job\" button below. Please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, three references, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, diversity statement, evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as a course syllabus), graduate transcripts, and any other relevant supporting documents through the online application system. If there are any questions, please send all inquiries by email to Patrick Nebl, Ph.D., Search Committee Chairperson, at patrick.nebl@elmhurst.edu. For full consideration, materials must be submitted by November 1. Position Status: Exempt Salary Range: $65,000 - $72,000. This is the expected salary range for this position. The actual salary offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Responsibilities Responsibilities for this position include course preparation, teaching, grading, and being available to students who have questions or require assistance; establishing a research program that actively includes undergraduate students; and service to the department and University. Other Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Supports the mission, vision, and values of Elmhurst University. Performs other faculty-related duties consistent with the department and University's mission and needs as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. (ABD with significant progress towards the degree and a completion date prior to August 2027 will also be considered) in a psychological discipline, demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring, and outstanding potential as a professor in a comprehensive liberal arts setting. Preferred Qualifications Applicant specialty should allow for the development of a successful research program at a primarily undergraduate institution that incorporates undergraduate students. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Additional Instructions for Applicants Interested candidates should electronically submit a 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) detailed list of three references, 4) statement of teaching philosophy, 5) statement of research interests and plans, 6) diversity statement, 7) evidence of teaching effectiveness, and 8) graduate transcripts. Applicants who proceed in the process will be asked to submit three letters of recommendation. If you have any questions, please contact Dr. Patrick Nebl in the Department of Psychology at patrick.nebl@elmhurst.edu. Review of credentials will begin November 1, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/9ED6FBEBE3/": {
      "title": "Library Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Library Services Coordinator. Academic Affairs / A.C. Buehler Library The Library Services Coordinator is responsible for various operational responsibilities, including opening the library, creating and maintaining the library’s multimedia content and social media presence, coordinating library building maintenance requests, maintaining the library’s physical collections, and purchasing and invoice processing. This position performs all circulation functions using current library management technologies, and models behavior that encourages a welcoming, efficient and effective experience for those who utilize the library and its resources. Position Status: Non - Exempt Salary Range: $20.00 - $21.00. This is the expected hourly range for this position. The hourly range offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Reporting and Supervisory Relationship(s): Reports to: Director, Library and Assistant Dean for Assessment and Accreditation Supervises : Serves as a back-up supervisor for Student Access Services Clerks Responsibilities Open the library on weekday mornings. Creates and maintains the library’s multimedia content and social media accounts, ensuring that the content is current, accurate, and consistent with library communication goals and University brand standards established by Marketing and Communications. Serves as the library building facilities contact and manages maintenance support requests, to include communicating status updates with appropriate library staff. Supports the library’s purchasing needs, to include monitoring supply inventory, placing orders when appropriate, keeping purchasing records, and processing invoices. Maintains the accurate order of the library’s physical collections, including shelf reading and reports related to items that are lost, missing, and claimed returned. Manages the Course Reserve collection, including serving as point of contact for faculty, and ensures basic editing of catalog records is completed to ensure that the collection is kept current. Assists with interlibrary loan functions, including preparing items for transit between libraries or shipment through mail. Provides general supervision and support for the Student Access Services Clerks in the absence of the Access Services Coordinator. Assists in managing the Textbook Collection. Collaborates with the Access Services team to process items being added to a collection once they have been cataloged, and to withdraw items weeded from a collection. Assists with all circulation functions, including material check-in and check-out, and study room reservations. Provides a high level of customer service for those wishing to use the library and its resources. Writes and maintains relevant procedures for the position. Troubleshoots technology issues when needed. Opens and closes the library when needed, which requires some flexibility to cover evening and/or weekend hours as needed and when adequate notice is provided. Other Responsibilities Supports the mission, vision, and values of Elmhurst University. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or demonstrated equivalent Demonstrated experience with social media in a professional environment At least two years of work experience in a customer service environment Excellent communication and customer service skills Must be able to exercise initiative and work independently Must have a strong attention to detail Must be able to perform work with a high level of accuracy Proficiency with Microsoft Office products Comfortable using various forms of technology Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is sometimes sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work requires occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 40 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Please submit cover letter, resume, and three references with contact information with the online application. The references should include name, phone number and email."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/5A2A8F136B/": {
      "title": "Night Custodian",
      "description": "Night Custodian. Facilities Management This position performs custodial work required for the cleaning and upkeep of buildings in accordance with the standards of the Night Custodial team, and ensures that completed work is of a high quality to maintain a clean and healthy learning and working environment for all members of the campus community. The hours for this position are 4:00 pm to 12:30 am. Position Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $17.50. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. Responsibilities Performs daily custodial duties as assigned including, but not limited to trash collection and removal; cleaning, sanitizing, and servicing restrooms; cleaning floors, stairs, and carpets; dusting; replacing light bulbs; cleaning windows and other glass surfaces; shoveling snow and de-icing building entrances. Learns to use and uses janitorial equipment including automatic scrubber, high-speed buffer, carpet extractor, upright vacuum, and low-speed floor scrubber. Maintains adequate stock of custodial supplies in assigned custodial closets. Inspects equipment and informs supervisor of any issues. Assists in setting up or taking down the set-up for special events as directed. This may include moving and removing large and heavy objects, such as, chairs, tables, and stages, either alone or with a coworker. Demonstrates proper ladder safety. Other Responsibilities Supports the mission, vision and values of Elmhurst University. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Follows all safety rules and regulations. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Basic knowledge of custodial equipment and supplies including their proper usage. Ability to work well independently and in a team. Willingness to work overtime as needed. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position require regular movement between indoor and outdoor campus locations, with exposure to varying weather conditions, including extreme heat and cold. Work is often physically demanding in nature and may require walking, navigating uneven or slippery surfaces, climbing stairs and ladders, bending, kneeling, and standing for extended periods. Required abilities include frequent use of fine motor skills to push, pull, or maneuver a range of equipment. Work requires regular lifting of objects up to 50 pounds, and occasional lifting of up to 100 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. Work Hours The hours for this position are 4:00 pm to 12:30 am. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Instructions to Applicants This position is designated by Elmhurst University as being safety sensitive. Per University policy, candidates for employment in safety-sensitive positions must comply with pre-employment drug testing, and employment in these positions is contingent upon completion of a drug test with satisfactory results. With consideration for the working conditions and physical requirements for this position, as described in the section above, a physical examination is required as well. Both the drug testing and physical examination are conducted at the University’s expense in an approved facility within one week of acceptance of a written offer of employment. Candidates may communicate with the testing facility and with Human Resources to explain any positive test results. For additional information regarding this policy, candidates may email Human Resources at hr@elmhurst.edu for assistance."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/696AC00357/": {
      "title": "Data Integrity and Reporting Specialist",
      "description": "Data Integrity and Reporting Specialist. Information Services The Data Integrity and Reporting Specialist is responsible for ensuring the accuracy, consistency, and reliability of organizational data while developing and maintaining reports that support business operations. This role collaborates with multiple departments to identify data quality issues, work with the AVP to implement corrective actions, and provide meaningful insights through data analysis and reporting. Position Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $23.00 - $25.50 per hour. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. The actual salary offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Reporting Relationship: Direct reporting relationship to: Assistant Vice President for Institutional Data and Applications Responsibilities Assists with data requests from leadership, academic and administrative departments, accreditation, regulatory reporting, surveys, and research initiatives. Collaborates with departments across the university to understand reporting requirements and provide data solutions. Monitors, validates, and maintains data quality and accuracy across multiple systems and databases; identifies, investigates, and resolves data discrepancies and integrity issues. Integrates and reconciles data from multiple systems to provide accurate, comprehensive reporting. Develops, generates, and distributes recurring and ad hoc reports for various campus departments. Automates recurring reports and manual data processes when appropriate to improve efficiency and reduce errors. Performs data audits and quality assurance reviews to ensure compliance with university data standards. Provides training and guidance to staff on accessing, interpreting, and appropriately using institutional data and reporting systems. Documents data management processes, procedures, and quality standards. Ensures compliance with data privacy, security, and regulatory requirements. Other Duties and Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Support the University's mission, vision, and values. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Information Systems, Data Analytics, Statistics, or a related field. Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel, including formulas, pivot tables, and data analysis functions. Experience working with databases, Unidata, SQL queries, and reporting tools. Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Excellent organizational, time management, written, and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems such as Ellucian Colleague. Familiarity with Technolutions Slate and Entrinsik Informer. Knowledge of data quality best practice. Understanding of data integration and automation tools. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here ."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/4F7255BB4C/": {
      "title": "Head Men’s Tennis Coach, Part-Time",
      "description": "Head Men’s Tennis Coach, Part-Time. Student Affairs / Intercollegiate Athletics The Head Men’s Tennis Coach is responsible for leading all facets of the Men’s Tennis Program. This individual will understand the mission of the NCAA, Division III, Elmhurst University Athletics, and the role of an athletic department in creating a positive environment for student-athletes. Position Status: Exempt Salary Range: $15,000. This is the expected salary range for this position. Reporting Relationship: Direct reporting relationship to: Director of Athletics Responsibilities Organizes and operates an effective and competitive Men’s Tennis Program. Coordinates recruitment of student-athletes. Attends and participates in all team planning sessions with coaching staff. Aids in the planning, organizing, and executing of all traditional season practice sessions for the program. Conducts on-court coaching during intercollegiate contests. Demonstrates a working knowledge of Elmhurst University, NCAA, and CCIW rules and regulations. Adheres to NCAA compliance regulations. Endorses and supports other sports within Elmhurst University Athletics. Interacts with other university constituencies, as appropriate, and actively participates in their events. Other Duties and Responsibilities Supports the mission, vision, and values of Elmhurst University. Supports the athletic department and the University’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree. Strong communication skills, both oral and written. Strong organizational skills and self-motivation. Special Notation: Staff members must possess a commitment and responsibility for adhering to all rules and regulations of Elmhurst University, the CCIW and the NCAA. Staff members must cooperate with and furnish the NCAA, the CCIW and/or Elmhurst University with truthful and complete information concerning involvement in or knowledge of rules violations. Any person who is found in violation of NCAA regulations shall be subject to disciplinary or correction actions a set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant or repeated violations. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in a variety of indoor and outdoor facilities, with regular exposure to varying weather conditions, including extended periods of extreme heat and cold. Work requires frequent districtwide, statewide, and out-of-state travel for recruiting or attending athletic competitions. Required abilities include walking, navigating uneven or slippery surfaces, bending, kneeling, and standing for extended periods; may require lifting and transporting equipment in excess of 50 pounds frequently and up to 100 pounds occasionally; and using fine motor skills to operate and maneuver a range of athletic or training equipment. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here ."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/4BC12A0946/": {
      "title": "Head Women’s Tennis Coach , Part-Time",
      "description": "Head Women’s Tennis Coach , Part-Time. Student Affairs / Intercollegiate Athletics The Head Women’s Tennis Coach is responsible for leading all facets of the Women’s Tennis Program. This individual will understand the mission of the NCAA, Division III, Elmhurst University Athletics, and the role of an athletic department in creating a positive environment for student-athletes. Position Status: Exempt Salary Range: $15,000. This is the expected salary range for this position. Reporting Relationship: Direct reporting relationship to: Director of Athletics Responsibilities Organizes and operates an effective and competitive Women's Tennis Program. Coordinates recruitment of student-athletes. Attends and participates in all team planning sessions with coaching staff. Aids in the planning, organizing, and executing of all traditional season practice sessions for the program. Conducts on-court coaching during intercollegiate contests. Demonstrates a working knowledge of Elmhurst University, NCAA, and CCIW rules and regulations. Adheres to NCAA compliance regulations. Endorses and supports other sports within Elmhurst University Athletics. Interacts with other university constituencies, as appropriate, and actively participates in their events. Other Duties and Responsibilities Supports the mission, vision, and values of Elmhurst University. Supports the athletic department and the University’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree. Strong communication skills, both oral and written. Strong organizational skills and self-motivation. Special Notation: Staff members must possess a commitment and responsibility for adhering to all rules and regulations of Elmhurst University, the CCIW and the NCAA. Staff members must cooperate with and furnish the NCAA, the CCIW and/or Elmhurst University with truthful and complete information concerning involvement in or knowledge of rules violations. Any person who is found in violation of NCAA regulations shall be subject to disciplinary or correction actions a set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant or repeated violations. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in a variety of indoor and outdoor facilities, with regular exposure to varying weather conditions, including extended periods of extreme heat and cold. Work requires frequent districtwide, statewide, and out-of-state travel for recruiting or attending athletic competitions. Required abilities include walking, navigating uneven or slippery surfaces, bending, kneeling, and standing for extended periods; may require lifting and transporting equipment in excess of 50 pounds frequently and up to 100 pounds occasionally; and using fine motor skills to operate and maneuver a range of athletic or training equipment. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here ."
