    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/43409FB8BF/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of CRM Processes and Analysis",
      "description": "Assistant Director of CRM Processes and Analysis. Admission The Assistant Director of CRM Processes and Analysis is a member of the admission technology team and serves as a technical and operational resource for the institution’s admission CRM. This position supports the development, administration, optimization, and ongoing improvement of the Technolutions Slate environment to advance enrollment goals and strengthen the student admission experience. The Assistant Director collaborates with campus partners to develop and maintain CRM workflows, reports, communications, and other tools while ensuring data accuracy, efficiency, and consistent processes. Position Status: Exempt Salary Range: $50,000-$55,000. This is the expected salary range for this position. The actual salary offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Responsibilities Supports the Director of CRM Processes and Analysis in the administration and ongoing development of the Technolutions Slate CRM to support admission operations and enrollment goals. Assists in developing, maintaining, testing, and deploying Slate workflows, rules, decisions, portals, forms, dashboards, campaigns, and communications. Develops and maintains regular reports, dashboards, and ad-hoc analyses to support admission operations and data-informed decision-making. Identifies opportunities to improve processes, increase efficiency, and make effective use of CRM technology and data. Provides day-to-day technical support for Slate users, including troubleshooting, prioritizing issues, and assisting with resolution. Develops user documentation and assists with training and support to promote consistent use of CRM tools and processes. Collaborates with campus partners, vendors, and other external partners on CRM enhancements, integrations, system updates, and new functionality. Assists with CRM-related projects, including system upgrades, migrations, testing, and implementation of new features. Maintains knowledge of Slate functionality, CRM best practices, and emerging technologies and assists in identifying opportunities for system enhancements. Other Responsibilities Supports the University’s mission, vision and values. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Performs other duties and completes special projects as needed and assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in information systems, computer science, business, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Demonstrated professional experience administering, developing, or supporting Technolutions Slate or a comparable CRM system. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications (Word, PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook). Strong analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and project coordination skills. Experience with reporting, data analysis, data quality, and data-informed decision-making. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to communicate technical concepts effectively to non-technical audiences. Ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Significant hands-on experience with Technolutions Slate in a college or university admissions, enrollment management, or student services environment. Proficiency in HTML, CSS, and SQL is a plus. Experience with Ellucian Colleague. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Please submit cover letter, resume, and three references with contact information with online application. The references should include name, phone number and email."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/5727369426/": {
      "title": "Advancement Operations Manager",
      "description": "Advancement Operations Manager. Institutional Advancement The Advancement Operations Manager serves as a key partner to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, providing high-level administrative, operational, and project management support for the Office of Institutional Advancement. This position oversees daily operations, coordinates projects, manages processes and budgets, and supports advancement-related activities, including fundraising, donor relations, alumni engagement, marketing, events, and advancement services. Serving as a liaison among campus stakeholders, alumni, donors, trustees, and external partners, the Advancement Operations Manager ensures effective communication, efficient operations, and execution of priorities. This role requires strong organizational, analytical, and relationship-management skills, the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, and a commitment to maintaining confidentiality and professionalism. Position Status: Non-Exempt, Full-Time (2080 Annual Hours) Salary Range: $22.00 - $24.00 per hour. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. The actual salary offered will depend on a candidate's experience and education, and departmental budget. Responsibilities Manages the daily operations of the Office of Institutional Advancement, ensuring efficient workflows, effective communication, and timely completion of priorities. Oversees office administration, purchasing, vendor coordination, records management, facilities requests, scheduling, conference room management, supply ordering, and office logistics. Serves as a front office contact for the Office of Institutional Advancement by greeting and welcoming visitors, responding to in-person, phone, and email inquiries, and providing backup support for the Alumni Relations phone line and shared inbox. Provides comprehensive administrative support to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement and coordinates and monitors divisional projects, timelines, and deliverables involving fundraising, donor relations, alumni engagement, marketing, advancement services, and events. Develops reports, presentations, meeting materials, and other documentation to support departmental planning, decision-making, and institutional reporting. Maintains budgets, processes requests and invoices for payment, and tracks budget activity. Coordinates the planning and execution of advancement events, donor stewardship activities, alumni programs, and fundraising initiatives, including event logistics, donor recognition programs, scholarship recognition and reporting, tribute gifts, and engagement activities. Administers advancement operations and data management functions, including non-profit charitable registration processes, compliance, and related documentation, CRM data entry, gift processing, record maintenance, reporting, and serving as a backup resource for Advancement Services. Coordinates and administers Board of Trustees Advancement Committee meetings, including scheduling, agenda preparation, board materials, minutes, and follow-up actions. Supervises and trains student employees, including assigning projects, monitoring performance, and ensuring completion of departmental tasks. Serves as a liaison between Institutional Advancement and campus departments, facilitating communication. Identifies opportunities for efficiency and process improvement and implements solutions. Maintains confidential donor, financial, and institutional information with the highest degree of discretion and professionalism. Other Duties and Responsibilities Supports the mission, vision and values of Elmhurst University. Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Three to five years of progressively responsible administrative or advancement-related experience. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines. Excellent organizational, analytical, problem-solving, and attention-to-detail skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to interact effectively with senior administrators, trustees, donors, alumni, faculty, staff, and external partners. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. Experience managing budgets and preparing reports. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and Outlook. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with CRM/database systems such as Raiser’s Edge NXT. Experience in donor relations, advancement services, or non-profit administration. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor setting with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here ."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/A4BAB4525B/": {
      "title": "Dispatcher, Part-Time",
      "description": "Dispatcher, Part-Time. Student Affairs / Public Safety The Dispatcher reliably and effectively functions as the in-office Public Safety representative, answering calls for service and communicating with patrol staff, Facilities Management personnel, Residence Life and other offices. Monitors alarms, access control and video security systems, and uses those systems to retrieve information in a timely manner. Maintains basic records associated with daily shift activities, and performs data entry of incident reports, parking records and other department information in an accurate and timely manner. In the event of an emergency situation, activates the University’s emergency procedures to protect life, prevent injury, protect property, and initiates emergency notifications. Position Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $19.00. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. Responsibilities Answers telephone calls, walk-up inquiries, and requests for service. Gathers appropriate information to assess situations for the proper response and articulates the necessary information to responding officers. Communicates with 911 personnel to request emergency assistance for police, fire and medical response to campus. Initiates emergency response procedures, and fulfills responsibilities in handling emergencies in accordance with department’s emergency procedures. Communicates with Public Safety and Facilities Management personnel by phone, radio and in-person, to resolve calls for service and emergency situations. Operates computer-based security systems, including video security systems, access control/alarm systems, emergency broadcast systems, fire alarm monitor, 911 call-alert computer, incident report database and dispatch call database. Uses capabilities of these systems to monitor activity, respond to and manage emergency situations, and collect information to support routine and emergency information needs. Issues parking permits and University ID’s, and maintains parking permit files and database. Performs data entry in the University’s main student/employee data system, and utilizes the system to acquire information needed for routine and emergency purposes. Prepares and enters information accurately in incident reports and work orders as needed. Electronically distributes reports according to department procedures. Interacts in a calm, professional and cordial manner with members of the campus community, including students, staff and faculty, as well as visitors to campus. Maintains positive working relationships with campus personnel and local emergency responders. Maintains accurate daily log of events. Performs occasional light administrative tasks. Other Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Supports the University’s mission, vision and values. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma. Ability to speak clearly and be understood via radio and phone communication. Ability to read comprehensively and apply both written and verbal directives. Normal hearing, due to the heavy volume of telephone and radio communication, audible alarms, and duties requiring monitoring of police/fire/EMS radio traffic. Strong command of the English language. Ability to maintain calm and professional demeanor during stressful or critical situations. Ability to communicate department/University policies and procedures in a professional manner. Strong computer skills, including solid experience with Microsoft Office products. Comfortable with technical equipment to include, radios, scanners, electronic access control, fire panels and PC based programs. Ability to work varying shifts, as required to meet departmental requirements. Preferred Qualifications Experience as a public safety/911 or campus security dispatcher. Work Hours: Weekend overnight shift openings : Shift #1: Friday 10:00 PM - Saturday 6:00 AM Shift #2: Saturday 10:00 PM - Sunday 6:00 AM Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor dispatch center environment, with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include clear speaking and active hearing for telephone, radio, and in person communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents and monitoring screens, and performing frequent tasks with repetitive fine motor skills, such as typing, writing, and operating dispatch systems and equipment. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Instructions to Applicants This position is designated by Elmhurst University as being safety sensitive. Per University policy, candidates for employment in safety-sensitive positions must comply with pre-employment drug testing, and employment in these positions is contingent upon completion of a drug test with satisfactory results. With consideration for the working conditions and physical requirements for this position, as described in the section above, a physical examination is required as well. Both the drug testing and physical examination are conducted at the University’s expense in an approved facility within one week of acceptance of a written offer of employment. Candidates may communicate with the testing facility and with Human Resources to explain any positive test results. For additional information regarding this policy, candidates may email Human Resources at hr@elmhurst.edu for assistance."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/85C81B232E/": {
      "title": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Dispatcher. Student Affairs / Public Safety The Dispatcher reliably and effectively functions as the in-office Public Safety representative, answering calls for service and communicating with patrol staff, Facilities Management personnel, Residence Life and other offices. This position monitors alarms, access control and video security systems, and uses those systems to retrieve information in a timely manner. Dispatchers maintain basic records associated with daily shift activities, and perform data entry of incident reports, parking records and other department information in an accurate and timely manner. In the event of an emergency situation, dispatchers activate the University’s emergency procedures to protect life, prevent injury, protect property, and initiate emergency notifications. Work Hours: Monday through Friday, 2:00 PM - 10:00 PM. Position Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $19.50. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. Responsibilities Answers telephone calls, walk-up inquiries, and requests for service. Gathers appropriate information to assess situations for the proper response and articulates the necessary information to responding officers. Communicates with 911 personnel to request emergency assistance for police, fire and medical response to campus. Initiates emergency response procedures, and fulfills responsibilities in handling emergencies in accordance with department’s emergency procedures. Communicates with Public Safety and Facilities Management personnel by phone, radio and in-person, to resolve calls for service and emergency situations. Operates computer-based security systems, including video security systems, access control/alarm systems, emergency broadcast systems, fire alarm monitor, 911 call-alert computer, incident report database and dispatch call database. Uses capabilities of these systems to monitor activity, respond to and manage emergency situations, and collect information to support routine and emergency information needs. Issues parking permits and University ID’s, and maintains parking permit files and database. Performs data entry in the University’s main student/employee data system, and utilizes the system to acquire information needed for routine and emergency purposes. Prepares and enters information accurately in incident reports and work orders as needed. Electronically distributes reports according to department procedures. Interacts in a calm, professional and cordial manner with members of the campus community, including students, staff and faculty, as well as visitors to campus. Maintains positive working relationships with campus personnel and local emergency responders. Maintains accurate daily log of events. Performs occasional light administrative tasks. Other Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Supports the University’s mission, vision and values. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma. Ability to speak clearly and be understood via radio and phone communication. Ability to read comprehensively and apply both written and verbal directives. Normal hearing, due to the heavy volume of telephone and radio communication, audible alarms, and duties requiring monitoring of police/fire/EMS radio traffic. Strong command of the English language. Ability to maintain calm and professional demeanor during stressful or critical situations. Ability to communicate department/University policies and procedures in a professional manner. Strong computer skills, including solid experience with Microsoft Office products. Comfortable with technical equipment to include, radios, scanners, electronic access control, fire panels and PC based programs. Ability to work varying shifts, as required to meet departmental requirements. Preferred Qualifications Experience as a public safety/911 or campus security dispatcher. Work Hours: Monday through Friday, 2:00 PM - 10:00 PM. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in an indoor dispatch center environment, with limited exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Work is often sedentary in nature and requires remaining in a stationary position for extended periods. Required abilities include clear speaking and active hearing for telephone, radio, and in person communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents and monitoring screens, and performing frequent tasks with repetitive fine motor skills, such as typing, writing, and operating dispatch systems and equipment. Work may require occasional lifting, bending, carrying, or otherwise moving objects weighing up to 15 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Instructions to Applicants This position is designated by Elmhurst University as being safety sensitive. Per University policy, employment in this position is contingent upon completion of a pre-employment drug test with satisfactory results. Testing is performed at the University’s expense in an approved facility within one week of acceptance of a written offer of employment. Candidates may communicate with the testing facility and with Human Resources to explain any positive test results. For additional information regarding this policy, candidates may email Human Resources at hr@elmhurst.edu for assistance."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/DAF75E2498/": {
      "title": "Services Specialist",
      "description": "Services Specialist. Facilities Management Under direct supervision, the Services Specialist performs set-ups, deliveries, cleaning, and upkeep of academic buildings. Regular schedule is Monday through Friday 2:30 pm – 11:00 pm. Weekends scheduled on a rotating basis, dependent upon demand. Position Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $17.50 - $18.50. This is the expected hourly rate for this position. Responsibilities Completes routine and special set-ups and take-downs throughout campus. Moves furniture as directed. Receives outside deliveries and disperses according to direction. Performs custodial duties throughout campus, including arranging classrooms, cleaning and restocking lavatories, as needed. Maintains service equipment, ensuring its good condition and proper use. Shovels snow and de-ices steps and walkways as directed. Reports equipment and items in buildings that require repair. Interfaces with work order and scheduling software for up-to-date information regarding daily tasks. Completes assigned work orders and, when needed, generates new work orders. Assists other departments as needed. Other Responsibilities Demonstrates a strong commitment to continuous improvement. Supports the University’s mission, vision and values. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Willingness to work overtime as needed, including weekends. Valid driver’s license. Competence with technology, such as work order or scheduling software. Ability to prioritize and organize tasks. Ability to work independently and with supervision. Ability to solve problems that arise during the evening shift. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position require regular movement between indoor and outdoor campus locations, with exposure to varying weather conditions, including extreme heat and cold. Work is often physically demanding in nature and may require walking, navigating uneven or slippery surfaces, climbing stairs and ladders, bending, kneeling, and standing for extended periods. Required abilities include frequent use of fine motor skills to push, pull, or maneuver a range of equipment. Work requires regular lifting of objects up to 50 pounds, and occasional lifting of up to 100 pounds. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Instructions to Applicants This position is designated by Elmhurst University as being safety sensitive. Per University policy, candidates for employment in safety-sensitive positions must comply with pre-employment drug testing, and employment in these positions is contingent upon completion of a drug test with satisfactory results. With consideration for the working conditions and physical requirements for this position, as described in the section above, a physical examination is required as well. Both the drug testing and physical examination are conducted at the University’s expense in an approved facility within one week of acceptance of a written offer of employment. Candidates may communicate with the testing facility and with Human Resources to explain any positive test results. For additional information regarding this policy, candidates may email Human Resources at hr@elmhurst.edu for assistance."
    },
    "https://apply.workable.com/elmhurst-edu/j/F6E0FCD394/": {
      "title": "Part-time Assistant Coaches (Ongoing Applications)",
      "description": "Part-time Assistant Coaches (Ongoing Applications). Student Affairs / Intercollegiate Athletics This is an ongoing posting to recruit temporary assistant coaches for the sports offered by Elmhurst University’s athletic program. Positions are temporary and seasonal, and openings may become available at various times throughout the year. Cover letters submitted with applications should clearly state which sport an applicant is applying to coach. A listing of Elmhurst University sports is available here . These positions assist a sport’s head coach with day-to-day operations of the program. Qualified applicants understand the mission of the NCAA, Division III athletics, and the role of an athletic department in creating a positive environment for student-athletes. Position Status: Exempt Salary Range: Temporary part-time assistant coaches are paid approximately $2,000 – $7,000 as a stipend per season, and may be rehired to work during future seasons. The actual stipend offered will depend on a candidate’s experience and education, length of applicable season including any pre-season and post-season work, required time commitment during the applicable season, and departmental budget. Responsibilities Assists the head coach in the organization and operation of an effective and competitive sport program. Supports the head coach in the coordination of recruiting student-athletes. Attends all pre-season conditioning and non-traditional season practices for the sport. Attends and participates in all team planning sessions with coaching staff. Aids in the planning, organization, and execution of all in-season practice sessions for the sport. Conducts coaching during intercollegiate contests as set and assigned by the head coach. Demonstrates a working knowledge of Elmhurst University, NCAA, and CCIW rules and regulations. Adheres to NCAA Compliance Regulations. Other Responsibilities Understands and supports the mission, vision, and values of Elmhurst University. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Strong oral and written communication skills. Organization skills and self-motivation. Working Conditions/Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position are primarily performed in a variety of indoor and outdoor facilities, with regular exposure to varying weather conditions, including extended periods of extreme heat and cold. Work requires frequent districtwide, statewide, and out-of-state travel for recruiting or attending athletic competitions. Required abilities include walking, navigating uneven or slippery surfaces, bending, kneeling, and standing for extended periods; may require lifting and transporting equipment in excess of 50 pounds frequently and up to 100 pounds occasionally; and using fine motor skills to operate and maneuver a range of athletic or training equipment. Qualified applicants who can perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodations will be considered. An overview of Elmhurst University benefits is available here . Instructions to Applicants This position is designated by Elmhurst University as being safety sensitive. Per University policy, employment in this position is contingent upon completion of a pre-employment drug test with satisfactory results. Testing is performed at the University’s expense in an approved facility within one week of acceptance of a written offer of employment. Candidates may communicate with the testing facility and with Human Resources to explain any positive test results. For additional information regarding this policy, candidates may email Human Resources at hr@elmhurst.edu for assistance. Special Notation Staff members must possess a commitment and responsibility for adhering to all rules and regulations of Elmhurst University, the CCIW and the NCAA. Staff members must cooperate with and furnish the NCAA, the CCIW and/or Elmhurst University with truthful and complete information concerning involvement in or knowledge of rules violations. Any person who is found in violation of NCAA regulations shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective actions as set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant or repeated violations."
    }
  },
